# No single-pass builds on anything non-trivial or financial

Run this project as an orchestrated team; verify adversarially before committing.
- **Planner** — decompose, read canonical sources, produce the step plan + linkage matrix + acceptance BEFORE code.
- **Builder** — one bounded change, fresh branch, per-change workflow. ONE builder per migration lane (never two migration authors at once — number collisions have happened).
- **Code-Review Agent (independent, mandatory)** — runs `.claude/skills/ih35-code-review`; reviews every diff vs Law of the Land, §10 linkage, schema landmines, design locks, security. MUST be a different agent than the builder. Unresolved high-severity findings block the PR.
- **Financial/Accounting Agent (mandatory for money-touching)** — runs `ih35-accounting-decisions`; audit-grade GL/ASC review (debits=credits, right accounts, reuse the poster, flags default-OFF until the owner's chat decision to turn on). Its unresolved high-severity findings **block the PR**. It does NOT gate the OWNER: enabling posting, flipping a flag or ratifying a treatment is the owner's sole DECISION (in chat, never a label), and this agent's job is to INFORM it with technical-correctness proof, never to approve or withhold merge. There is no CPA sign-off in this system. **No holds, no `JORGE-APPROVED` — OWNER LAW 2026-08-03.**
- **GUARD/Verifier** — proves each item live (throwaway PG apply-twice → coder applies on Neon themselves, FULL access → re-prove on prod with RLS bypass AFTER merge → deploy SHA → verify:* guards). Produces the `acceptance[]` evidence.
Fan out to be comprehensive; converge with independent verification (≥1 independent verifier per financial finding); loop-until-dry on audits. Never let the builder review or verify its own work. Log anything dropped/deferred.

